Create a banner section using this layered technique:

Base color: Solid gold/bronze background — 
#6B4E1E

Layer structure (back to front):

Photo — positioned to fill the banner, but masked so it's fully invisible on the left ~40% and fades in smoothly until fully visible by ~70% across
Color tint — the same gold color (
#6B4E1E) applied over the photo using mix-blend-mode: color at ~55% opacity, so the photo's tones shift toward gold/bronze instead of looking like a plain, un-blended photo cutout
Wavy line texture — a few thin, curved, flowing lines (like loose sine waves) in white at very low opacity (4–6%), spanning the full width and height of the banner, layered on top of everything
Content — heading text in white, positioned on the left side where the pure gold color still shows

CSS technique for the fade:

css
.photo {
  mask-image: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent 0%, transparent 40%, black 70%);
}
.tint {
  background: #6B4E1E;
  mix-blend-mode: color;
  opacity: 0.55;
}
